  "status": "theorem_candidate_passed",
  "theorem": "The admitted G900 construction supplies an exact ordered 15-by-60 product, a native base-60 vertex enumeration, and a signed carrier system reducing the unsigned G15 automorphism group of order 120 to a residual order-two symmetry. The transposed formula f_T(slot,local)=15*local+slot is an exact bijection into the first 900 B32K wire indices and exposes the G15 slot as the B32K anchor residue. Once f_T is chosen, the residual involution transports to an exact covariant address action rho_tau. However, neither f_T nor rho_tau is declared by the pinned G900 or B32K sources, no cross-source slot-to-anchor matching relation is present, and no bridge acts on the reflected five-offset D5 torsor. Therefore current G900 narrows the missing bridge to a coherent candidate enrichment but does not natively select the unresolved premultiplier D5 offset."
